WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:00.939
Quick recap.

00:00:01.276 --> 00:00:01.926
Two rules.

00:00:02.553 --> 00:00:04.875
Rule one: new pieces only join the

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:05.816
3-prime end.

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:08.672
So new DNA grows 5-prime to 3-prime.

00:00:09.299 --> 00:00:11.818
Rule two: DNA polymerase can't start from

00:00:11.864 --> 00:00:12.282
nothing.

00:00:12.909 --> 00:00:14.941
A short RNA primer comes first.

00:00:15.568 --> 00:00:16.949
Like a first domino that starts the

00:00:16.984 --> 00:00:17.379
chain.

00:00:18.006 --> 00:00:20.502
New DNA grows 5-prime to 3-prime, and

00:00:20.549 --> 00:00:21.710
it needs a primer to start.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.184
Let's see what you remember.
